// ── Pages: the one authority to ask the kernel for huge pages. A program that never handles Srs.Pages (only main may,
// Ty.worldHandler) gets no advice until its Arena makes a second 32 MiB reservation: the Arena arms the gate itself
// (a program past 32 MiB pays the one /proc/vmstat read; a small one pays nothing). The Arena advises each fresh
// reservation while the gate is On: main (or the Arena) arms it with the machine-wide count of failed huge-page faults
// (/proc/vmstat thp_fault_fallback), and it shuts for good once more than
// Srs.Pages.limit() failed since (each failure cost a compaction stall). The gate is the rt_globals words tag, base and
// seen (the last count read); only Srs.Gate.arm and Srs.Gate.shut write tag, and nothing turns a Shut gate On again.
// A constructor with a field allocates in a Region and the prelude fns have none, so the gate enum has no field: base is a word.
enum Srs.Gate:
  case Srs.GateIdle
  case Srs.GateOn
  case Srs.GateShut

